From: LuneOS <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] gallivm: check builder.create() for NULL before using it

lp_build_create_jit_compiler_for_module() dereferences the ExecutionEngine
returned by builder.create() in the cache_out and JITEVENTS blocks, and only
then tests it for NULL - eight lines too late. When MCJIT creation fails the
process segfaults instead of taking the error path that is already written
immediately below, which frees the generated code and returns the message
LLVM put in Error.

Reproducible by running any llvmpipe client under qemu-arm user-mode emulation,
where MCJIT creation fails for the emulated target:

  signal : 11 SIGSEGV (bad memory access)
  si_addr: 0x00000000
  pc     : /usr/lib/libgallium-26.2.0.so + 0x4ffac6
            -> src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_misc.cpp:635
                 JIT->setObjectCache(objcache);

Moving the check to immediately after create() turns that into the intended
"Could not create LLVM JIT" error return. It does not make the JIT succeed -
that is a separate LLVM-under-emulation problem - but the caller gets to handle
it rather than dying.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_misc.cpp b/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_misc.cpp
index 51fdafa0bd3..ac920d1cfa3 100644
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_misc.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_misc.cpp
@@ -629,6 +629,13 @@ lp_build_create_jit_compiler_for_module(LLVMExecutionEngineRef *OutJIT,
    ExecutionEngine *JIT;
 
    JIT = builder.create();
+   if (!JIT) {
+      lp_free_generated_code(*OutCode);
+      *OutCode = 0;
+      delete MM;
+      *OutError = strdup(Error.c_str());
+      return 1;
+   }
 
    if (cache_out) {
       LPObjectCache *objcache = new LPObjectCache(cache_out);
@@ -640,15 +647,9 @@ lp_build_create_jit_compiler_for_module(LLVMExecutionEngineRef *OutJIT,
    JITEventListener *JEL = JITEventListener::createIntelJITEventListener();
    JIT->RegisterJITEventListener(JEL);
 #endif
-   if (JIT) {
-      *OutJIT = wrap(JIT);
-      return 0;
-   }
-   lp_free_generated_code(*OutCode);
-   *OutCode = 0;
-   delete MM;
-   *OutError = strdup(Error.c_str());
-   return 1;
+
+   *OutJIT = wrap(JIT);
+   return 0;
 }
 
 
